dnswire
------------------------------------------
A C library for encoding/decoding different DNS encapsulations and transporting
them over different protocols.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libdnswire-devel-0.5.1-1bl1
  libdnswire1-0.5.1-1bl1
  libprotobuf-c-devel-1.5.2-1bl2
  libprotobuf-c1-1.5.2-1bl2
  libtinyframe-devel-0.1.2-1bl1
  libtinyframe0-0.1.2-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.9-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.10-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libprotobuf-c-devel-1.5.2-1bl2
  libtinyframe-devel-0.1.2-1bl1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  libuv-devel-1.53.0-1
  make-4.4.1-2
  protobuf-c-1.5.2-1bl2

Canonical website:
  https://codeberg.org/DNS-OARC/dnswire

Canonical download:
  https://codeberg.org/DNS-OARC/dnswire.git

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack dnswire-0.5.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./dnswire-0.5.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/dnswire-0.5.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/dnswire-0.5.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libdnswire1-0.5.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libdnswire-devel-0.5.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(dnswire)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/dnswire.README
